# Sample desk order gate

`?view=sample` serves **Nova Marketing Sample Data** — a screenshot/marketing desk built
from fixtures. It must never reach a broker. This rule exists because a partial
guard once shipped and was strictly more dangerous than no guard at all.

## The invariant

Every code path that writes to a broker endpoint **must refuse when
`isSampleView()` is true**, and a composite path must refuse **as one unit**.

Guarded doors today:

| Door | File |
|---|---|
| Place / cancel-all | `frontend/src/ibkr/placeOrder.ts` |
| Cancel one | `frontend/src/ibkr/cancelOrder.ts` |
| Flatten account | `frontend/src/ibkr/flattenAccount.ts` |
| Emergency KILL composite | `frontend/src/ibkr/emergencyKill.ts` |

## Why all-or-nothing, not per-leg

`emergencyKill.ts` composes `L0 + desk lock → cancel → flatten`. Cancel-before-flatten
exists so a resting order cannot fill **during** the flatten.

A guard on `cancelAllWorkingOrders` alone removes the protective leg and keeps the
destructive one — the account still gets flattened, now with working orders left live.
That is worse than guarding nothing. `runEmergencyKillOnce` therefore returns on
`sampleKillRefusal()` **before** any leg runs, and the caller surfaces the refusal so
the operator is told nothing happened rather than reading a refusal mid-flatten.

**If you guard one leg of a composite, you must guard the composite.**

## Adding a new order door

Any new function that POSTs / DELETEs / PATCHes a broker or bot endpoint:

1. Guard it at the `novaFetch` call site — not at the UI, which can be bypassed and
   which future callers will not share.
2. Add it to the table above in the same commit.
3. Add a wiring test under `frontend/src/sample_data/` asserting the transport boundary
   is never reached on the sample route.
4. If it is a leg of a composite, guard the composite instead and say so.

Not every `novaFetch` writer under `frontend/src/ibkr/` is a broker order door —
`acknowledgeVerification.ts`, `GatewayModeCapsule.tsx` and `TradingPrerequisitesGate.tsx`
write desk/session state, not orders. Decide by **what the endpoint does to the
account**, not by which directory the file sits in.

## Boundaries this rule does NOT move

Invariant #7 is unchanged: orders still flow only through gated `backend/ibkr/`,
`IBKR_ENABLED` / `IBKR_ORDERS_ENABLED` / `IBKR_LIVE_TRADING_CONFIRMED` still apply, and
`auto_live` remains NO-GO. This is a client-side refusal on one marketing route; it is a
second lock, never a replacement for the backend gate.

## Wording

"Nova Marketing Sample Data" or "sample", in code identifiers and user-visible copy.
Never "fake", "mock" or "dummy".

Related: #357 (the desk), AGENTS.md Invariant #5 (SOP before code) and Invariant #7
(broker execution gate).
